 PLATFORM-005 does not authenticate principals or own session truth (PLATFORM-003/Foundation), does not qualify/route capabilities (PLATFORM-006), does not own observability truth (PLATFORM-012), does not own domain/durable-work truth, does not own PostgreSQL state, and cannot authorize tool/effect execution. Navigation visibility is never execution authorization.
 
 ## Projection law
-The client projection contains only bounded shell-safe fields. It omits session identifiers, principal identity, role sets, authentication generation, CSRF/device bindings, server authorization rules, capability policy internals, domain data and secrets. Invalid/expired session binding, network loss or stale loads clear dynamic navigation. UNKNOWN upstream health is degraded, never optimistic ONLINE.
+The client projection contains only bounded shell-safe fields. It omits session identifiers, principal identity, role sets, authentication generation, CSRF/device bindings, server authorization rules, capability policy internals, domain data and secrets. Invalid/expired session binding, expired projection TTL, network loss or stale loads clear dynamic navigation. The browser must fail closed at `expiresAt` even if no network/visibility event occurs. UNKNOWN upstream health is degraded, never optimistic ONLINE.
 
 ## Route law
 Work-surface routes are origin-relative, non-API, normalized and bounded. Absolute/protocol-relative/credential-bearing/fragment/backslash/traversal/encoded traversal or encoded separator/null forms fail closed. DOM labels are rendered with textContent only.
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 Authenticated shell projection reads are same-origin, credential-bound, no-store, non-redirecting and byte-bounded before JSON parsing. Sensitive/authenticated responses are never admitted to browser cache authority.
 
 ## Offline/service-worker law
-Only a fixed digest-bound non-sensitive static allowlist may enter Cache API. Service-worker fetch interception is same-origin GET only and excludes /api. Static cache population omits credentials. Updates activate only through SYSTEM_MASTER_ACTIVATE_UPDATE; emergency SYSTEM_MASTER_UNREGISTER_AND_PURGE unregisters the worker and clears owned caches.
+Only a fixed digest-bound non-sensitive static allowlist may enter Cache API. Cached shell assets must also expire at the declared offline-policy maximum age (24 hours for the conservative SMR018 policy); missing/future/stale cache timestamps fail closed. Service-worker fetch interception is same-origin GET only and excludes /api. Static cache population omits credentials. Updates activate only through SYSTEM_MASTER_ACTIVATE_UPDATE; emergency SYSTEM_MASTER_UNREGISTER_AND_PURGE unregisters the worker and clears owned caches.
 
 ## Persistence decision
 PLATFORM-005 creates no PostgreSQL table or durable canonical store. Browser Cache API state is disposable, bounded, non-sensitive shell-only projection state.
